node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
.tmp/
.DS_Store

# Frame recordings from `sim:run --record` (G-017). The README's own example writes 58 MB
# of run.ndjson into the repo root, and a recording is a derived artefact of a seed and a
# command log — it is regenerated in seconds and must never be committed.
*.ndjson

# I3 gate-bite probes. AT G-039b-β2 `content-gate.test.ts` STOPPED WRITING THESE INTO THE
# REPOSITORY — the probe now lives in a materialised tree under the system temp directory,
# because a file inside `packages/sim/src` is inside a tsconfig include and a concurrent run's
# `tsc` could glob it and then find it gone (TS6053). The pattern stays as a third line of
# defence: if anybody ever reaches for the old shape again, the probe still cannot be
# committed. Nothing in the tree writes one today, and `content-gate.test.ts` asserts that.
*.gate-probe.ts

# SVG frame recordings from `pnpm --filter @hotelsim/game record` (G-035). Same rule as the
# ndjson above and for the same reason: a recording is a derived artefact of a seed and a
# command log, it is regenerated in seconds, and a run of 2,880 ticks writes twenty-six
# frames plus a contact sheet. Watch it, write what you saw in `JOURNAL.md`, delete it.
recording/

# A red row's own output, kept by `pnpm verify` so an intermittent failure can be diagnosed
# rather than re-run (G-039a). Derived from one run of one tree; the next run rewrites it.
# It exists because three sightings of an intermittent row produced no captured text at all.
.verify-logs/

# The `pnpm verify` mutual-exclusion lock (G-039b-beta2). One verify at a time per tree: two
# concurrent runs are two full worker pools on one core budget, which is the regime that
# produced five unexplained `Test timed out` rows. Created and removed by tools/gates/verify.mjs
# and stolen from a dead owner on the next run, so it never needs to be committed or cleaned.
.verify-lock/

# Critic transfer material (G-059). Untracked working scratch that `git add -A` would land —
# 5.4 MB of it at the sweep that found this. It is derived from the tree it describes and is
# regenerated by re-running the sweep, so it is ignored for `*.ndjson`'s reason exactly.
_review_transfer/
